Recommendation 4: DSS should ensure that only costs incurred by a program are charged to the program by:
a.	Establishing written cost allocation guidance for vendors reimbursed based on incurred costs; 
b.	Requiring vendors to submit cost allocation methodologies that are consistent with such guidance, for each cost subject to allocation;
c.	Training staff to properly review invoices and to test for appropriate allocation of costs; and
d.	Conducting sample-based reviews of allocated costs to ensure claims for allocated costs are reasonable and program related.

Recommendation 5: DSS should strengthen its procedures for reviewing claims prior to making payment by:
a.	Ensuring staff who are responsible for contract oversight are familiar with City fiscal policy and contractual payment terms and conditions; 
b.	Comparing claimed costs with approved budgets and holding vendors to approved budgeted amounts; 
c.	Training invoice review staff to spot expenses claimed on behalf of subcontractors to ensure the use of such subcontractors have been approved; and
d.	Conducting interim and/or real time reviews to determine whether invoices submitted to DSS are adequately supported and comply with contractual terms.

Recommendation 1: RCPA should maintain sufficient and complete records documenting each residence search to accurately identify decedents’ assets, such as: 
a.	Initial Entry Reports with information properly filled in and signed by the required RCPA and other personnel;
b.	Video that captures all essential activities of the search process and photographs that document the valuable items identified during the searches;
c.	A detailed inventory list for each estate following the property search to correctly document all assets; and
d.	A log to document every visit to a decedent’s residence, the individuals who entered the residence, and the reason for the entry.

Recommendation 5: RCPA should require Victorian Brothers to improve its accountability of estate sales and auctioned items by:
a.	Maintaining a list of valuable items, by estate, before sending to the auction house or conducting the estate sale;
b.	Listing the sales price of each item;
c.	Maintaining records for each item sold and the name of the purchasers;
d.	Using a cash register to safeguard sales proceeds;
e.	Reconciling the inventory and the sold items with the remaining inventory; and
f.	Providing detailed invoices listing the items sold or services rendered when requesting payments from RCPA.

Recommendation 1: DVS should ensure all current and newly hired staff are trained on the newly created written policies and Standard Operating Procedures, and are following all procedures, including: 
•	intake and application handling process; 
•	tracking intake and documenting veteran’s housing assistance requests;
•	tracking the move out of veterans who are transitioning out of shelters/housing insecurity;
•	tracking aftercare services (including the frequency interval) and documenting aftercare services provided; and
•	documentation protocols and maintaining consistent notes that DVS staff input for VetConnectNYC housing assistance requests and aftercare services.

Recommendation 4: NYCPS should develop NYCPS-wide training and outreach programs to:
a. 	Increase participation in all NYCPS food waste reduction programs;
b. 	Encourage information and idea sharing, and create opportunities for collaboration, amongst sustainability coordinators across the school system; 
c. 	Improve the percentage of food waste that is captured as potential compost; and
d. 	Reduce contamination to ensure that what is captured is compostable. 
e. 	Conduct on-site visits to schools to verify that they comply with the composting and recycling requirements by having recycling and composting bins properly placed in cafeterias and classrooms.
